":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T06:42:03-07:00","id":1483308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1483290-crystal-prison?p=1483300#post1483300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i believe it only appeared as one of the arts of the Merfolk in Blood Dimmed Tide, but C20 drew on it for Winter among its four added Seasonal Arts</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In fact C20, as far as I know, only &quot;recycled&quot; the level 5. Crystal Prison, the power I'm mentioning, is the level 4 power of the Art. Kryos you find in Blood Dimmed Tides, pp. 77-80.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T18:53:39-07:00","id":1483769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1483290-crystal-prison?p=1483308#post1483308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact C20, as far as I know, only &quot;recycled&quot; the level 5. Crystal Prison, the power I'm mentioning, is the level 4 power of the Art. Kryos you find in Blood Dimmed Tides, pp. 77-80.</div> </div> </div> </div>In C20 it became more powerful and versatile as the level 5 of <b>Winter</b>: <i><b>Stasis</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Going by the original, I wouldn't give any such a roll, the same way it isn't allowed for the Changelings to begin with. It doesn't mean you can't break the ice once formed, though, successes in Crystal Prison determine thickness, but the ice is otherwise normal, so that's the reason why it gives no resisting roll: nothing in the victim prevents the Art from completion, but nothing in the Art prevents the victim from breaking or melting the ice.<br /> <br /> But I would recommend to use Winter instead of Kryos, as it is basically Kryos improved. In that case Stasis is more powerful but does give a resisting roll for supernaturals at the cost of 1 WP, you roll Stamina Dif 9 (it is still quite hard, but hey, it is level 5 now, and won't kill).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}